{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1576873633,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDExODQ2MjQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3953","origin":"github"},"title":"Silent failures due to interaction between custom_result_renderer() and log.result-level","message":"Some of our `custom_result_renderer` definitions return early if a `status` other than \"ok\" is encountered.  For example, here's the beginning of the `RunProcedure.custom_result_renderer`:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/b1f33d17bd2630bf202dcf584d94acb9670c6cd1/datalad/interface/run_procedure.py#L468-L474\n\nAs the comment suggests, these checks exist to avoid double reporting of errors and warnings, things like\n\n```\n$ datalad run-procedure not-there\n[WARNING] Cannot find procedure with name 'not-there' [run_procedure(not-there)]\nrun_procedure(impossible): not-there [Cannot find procedure with name 'not-there']\n```\n\nIn response to the same double reporting concern, 60d088feb (ENH: Introduce datalad.log.result-level config switch, 2019-10-06) made it easy to demote the logging messages.  While both the `custom_result_renderer` check and `log.result-level` seem fine enough on their own, they can squelch all messages when combined.  To continue with `run_procedure` as an example, running\n\n```sh\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\ncd \"$(mktemp -d --tmpdir dl-XXXXXXX)\"\ndatalad create \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261\n\ngit config datalad.log.result-level debug\ndatalad run-procedure not-there\n```\n\nleads to no log message being shown and no result being rendered.\n\nWith the introduction of `log.result-level`, we should revisit these `custom_result_renderer` checks.\n\n---\n\nBased on some quick grepping, here's a list of commands with a `custom_result_renderer` that returns early when given a status other than \"ok\":\n\n- `metadata`\n- `run_procedure`\n- `siblings`\n- `status` (also used by `diff`)","files":null}]}